   "daf": "67a",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "זֶה הַכְּלָל, כֹּל שֶׁבַּהֲנָאָתוֹ בְּנוֹתֵן טַעַם כּוּ׳. אָמַר רַב יְהוּדָה אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: הָכִי הִלְכְתָא.",
   "en": "§ It is stated in the mishna: «This is the principle: Anything that benefits» from a forbidden item «imparting flavor» to it, i.e., the forbidden item contributes a positive taste to it, is forbidden, and anything that does not benefit from a forbidden item imparting flavor to it is permitted, e.g., forbidden vinegar that fell onto split beans, as the flavor imparted by the vinegar does not enhance the taste of the beans. «Rav Yehuda says» that «Shmuel says: This is the halakha.»"
  }
 ],
